  "acceptance_notes": [
    "Fresh full headless run 40779930742 checks Windows/Linux, Native/Java, BASE/PINOUT and both loaders on the corrected runtime. No failed or interrupted attempt is relabeled.",
    "The separate graphical cohort retains twelve real client scenarios, exact newly exported archives, helper sources, accepted powered readings, Save and Quit and dedicated save/stop outcomes.",
    "A local starter proof locator stopped the first client campaign before either SDK starter launched. Its original failed report and ten complete cases remain retained; only the two missing starter cases were executed in a fresh attempt after verifying the exact CI proof bytes.",
    "The original candidate exposed a recursive API terminal/CEE infrastructure startup load. Its failed evidence is preserved. Corrected terminal binding and a new pre-tick regression passed before these fresh lanes.",
    "Workshop startup storage-adapter rejection warnings are retained in the client reports. The same warnings and occurrence counts exist in the accepted 0.2.3 clients; the corrected startup replay does not introduce or suppress them.",
    "Ground reload checks use native blocking disk work before entity readiness assertions under uncapped GameTest ticks. Electrical assertions, actual unload proof, tick bounds, launcher deadlines and watchdog stay unchanged.",
    "The gameplay jar excludes GameTests and fixtures. All coverage remains in the separate companion. Public API 1.0.0 and all native libraries are unchanged.",
    "The 14,650-node benchmark native save bytes are preserved; only release/jar labels changed. No performance benchmark was run, and 20 TPS remains uncertified.",
    "Headless train fixtures cover actual movement across overhead contacts, native PG meter availability and dimension-owned state. The general client scenarios do not certify all train audio or dimension travel.",
    "Current installation guides and release metadata are frozen separately after acceptance. Every runtime entry and companion byte is unchanged; actual full headless and client execution records retain source de1491e480337e2cfd3e0b6382f59ee2150906f7."
  ],
